<title>USA: TWA pilots say suit dismissed by judge.</title>
<headline>TWA pilots say suit dismissed by judge.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans World Airlines Inc's pilots said a federal judge threw out the union's lawsuit against the airline, saying the case does not fall under the jurisdiction of the federal court.</p>
<p>The pilots union had filed suit against TWA, contesting the calculation of certain pay and work rules.</p>
<p>&quot;But we are pleased to report that we will achieve our primary objective in the lawsuit. That is, a hearing before an arbitrator,&quot; the Air Line Pilots Union said in a recorded message to its members.</p>
<p>The union said the hearing will be held this week. Additional details were not immediately available.</p>
<p>(( New York newsdesk 212-859-1610 ))</p>
</text>
